# Testing Standards

Do not consider a feature complete because it works on the happy path.

## Preserve the learning loop

Regularly test:

launch
→ open lesson
→ read exercise
→ edit code
→ Run
→ Check
→ fail
→ receive feedback
→ request hints
→ fix solution
→ pass
→ unlock next lesson
→ close app
→ reopen app
→ progress remains

## Learner code cases

Always preserve behavior for:

valid code

syntax errors

runtime errors

no output

multiple print statements

infinite loops

alternative valid solutions

incorrect types

incorrect values

unexpected but valid Python

## Platform

The primary local user platform is Windows.

Do not assume POSIX behavior is sufficient.

Cross-platform process management must explicitly consider Windows.

## GUI

GUI work must not block the main UI thread during learner code execution.

Tk/Qt widget operations must occur on the GUI thread unless the framework explicitly guarantees otherwise.

## Progress

Test:
- missing progress file
- valid progress
- malformed JSON
- partially malformed data
- reset progress
- saved drafts
- completion state
- hints used
- attempt counts

## Regression behavior

Every meaningful bug fix should add a regression test where practical.

Run the complete automated test suite before declaring significant work finished.

Do not delete or weaken tests merely to make a change pass.
